1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:11,083
The Ortiz family saw a sample board: they want natural oak cabinets on the back wall, with paint-grade MDF doors and drawer fronts. The job is already built.

2
00:00:11,083 --> 00:00:15,140
Before Job-1 that meant opening every cabinet. Now: Cabinets tab → Change materials.

3
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:28,361
Boards by role (carcass, fronts, backs, drawer boxes) and bands by group. Each says what the job uses now. Anything left at "Keep as is" is not touched.

4
00:00:28,361 --> 00:00:35,085
Roles come from how the app builds each cabinet, not from part names, so a "door" is always a door and a filler follows the fronts.

5
00:00:35,085 --> 00:00:44,605
Carcass: PB18-OAK, the oak melamine with grain. Fronts: MDF18, paint grade.

6
00:00:44,605 --> 00:00:54,036
Bands follow the look: oak ABS on the carcass front edges. Paint-grade MDF doors get no band, they are sprayed.

7
00:00:54,036 --> 00:00:59,101
And a test: put the drawer boxes on 18 mm board, to see what the check says.

8
00:00:59,101 --> 00:01:11,017
Only the back wall changes. Chosen cabinets → Select by wall: Back wall. The left-wall cabinets stay white.

9
00:01:11,017 --> 00:01:18,365
Preview first. Nothing is applied yet.

10
00:01:18,365 --> 00:01:28,941
The warning: TANDEM slides take drawer sides up to 16 mm. The same check as the cabinet editor; you can still apply, but the warning stays on the job.

11
00:01:28,941 --> 00:01:37,869
Sheets before → after, per board: an estimate from the automatic nest, so you see the material cost of the change before you make it.

12
00:01:37,869 --> 00:01:48,610
Every part that changes: board old → new, edges that change, and any size that changes with a board thickness.

13
00:01:48,610 --> 00:02:08,662
That warning is a real problem, so set Drawer boxes back to Keep as is (PB16 white) and preview again.

14
00:02:08,662 --> 00:02:13,640
Clean. Apply.

15
00:02:13,640 --> 00:02:18,923
Done in one step. The cards show the oak carcass; the left wall stays white.

16
00:02:18,923 --> 00:02:33,949
Cut list: oak and MDF parts now, and the oak band on the carcass edges.

17
00:02:33,949 --> 00:02:40,317
Nesting re-runs: oak sheets with the grain kept along each part, and an MDF sheet for the fronts.

18
00:02:40,317 --> 00:02:46,037
Quote follows too: the board line now counts oak and MDF sheets.

19
00:02:46,037 --> 00:02:54,258
Customer changes their mind again? Cabinets tab → Undo material change. One click puts every part back.

20
00:02:54,258 --> 00:03:00,021
All white again. (Undo lives while the app is open; anything you edited since is left alone.)

21
00:03:00,021 --> 00:03:05,783
So: pick per role, choose the cabinets, preview parts, sheets and warnings, apply, and keep Undo as your safety net.
